{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":27581,"name":null,"username":"it44","avatar_template":"/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/i/74df32/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-11-19T10:45:02.756Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eApplicant: it44 · GitHub: agentcontrolmap/ckb-script-fixtures (public repo; links will follow in a reply once the forum allows them) · Contact: replies in this thread\u003cbr\u003e\nFunding requested: $600 USD equivalent, paid in USDI · Duration: 4 weeks · License: MIT\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e1. What this is\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nOpen-source test fixtures (Rust, ckb-testtool, runnable with \u003ccode\u003ecargo test\u003c/code\u003e) that turn review findings about CKB scripts into executable, reproducible checks: a “naive” version that accepts the bad transaction and a “hardened” version that rejects it, so a maintainer sees the issue and the fix in one run. Not a scanner, not an audit, not a new security framework.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e2. Existing work (not requested for funding)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEscrow review, five points (group inputs, refund/release race, fee burn on permissionless refund, minimum-capacity remainder, terms not validated at creation): my post \u003cspan class=\"hashtag-raw\"\u003e#2\u003c/span\u003e in the “Spark Program | CKB Escrow Security Test Kit” topic (topic 11150).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePublic repo agentcontrolmap/ckb-script-fixtures with the first fixtures already in place (seven scenarios on a toy escrow lock, naive vs hardened; the README lists what they do NOT show). CI passes on a clean checkout: workflow run \u003cspan class=\"hashtag-raw\"\u003e#3\u003c/span\u003e in the repo’s Actions tab.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePrice-feed question (upper bound on the update timestamp): my post \u003cspan class=\"hashtag-raw\"\u003e#3\u003c/span\u003e in the “Asset Price Oracle on Nervos Network” topic (topic 10800). The maintainer’s reply (post \u003cspan class=\"hashtag-raw\"\u003e#5\u003c/span\u003e) agrees the scenario is valid for the deployed \u003ccode\u003eprice_feed_type\u003c/code\u003e and says an on-chain bound is worth investigating.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e3. Deliverables (4 weeks)\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eM1 (week 1): minimum-capacity remainder fixture on a local dev chain, plus CI on the repo as it stands. Acceptance: clean checkout, \u003ccode\u003ecargo test\u003c/code\u003e passes, README says what each fixture shows and does NOT show.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eM2 (week 2): fixture for the feed-timestamp scenario against a local copy of the logic, only if public source allows a standalone reproduction; otherwise publish why and the exact missing input.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eM3 (week 3): the same method on ONE further public CKB script with its owner’s consent; negative results published too.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eM4 (week 4): final report: planned vs done, limitations, owner feedback if given.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e4. Budget\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nM1 remaining work $100 · M2 $200 · M3 $200 · M4 report $100. Total $600. The fixtures already published are not charged. No recurring costs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e5. Verification\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nEverything is reproducible from a clean checkout; every claim in the report is tagged as run, read-only, or unverified. Weekly updates in this thread.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e6. Risks\u003c/strong\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\nOwners may not engage (then published as independent work, disclosed); fixtures show the behaviour of the code given, not an audit or guarantee; scope limited to the listed scripts. A negative result is still reported.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-11-19T10:45:02.756Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":15,"readers_count":14,"score":48.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":11264,"topic_slug":"spark-program-ckb-script-regression-fixtures-reproducible-tests-for-review-findings","display_username":null,"primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[{"id":2,"count":1}],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":4523,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/spark-program-ckb-script-regression-fixtures-reproducible-tests-for-review-findings/11264/1","babel_translations_meta":[{"language":"es","status":"completed","source_language":"en"},{"language":"zh-cn","status":"completed","source_language":"en"}],"show_translation_widget":true,"show_translation_button":true,"babel_detected_locale":"en","reactions":[{"id":"heart","type":"emoji","count":1}],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":1,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false,"can_translate":false}],"stream":[27581]},"timeline_lookup":[[1,2]],"suggested_topics":[{"fancy_title":"CKB Eco Fund | Spark program Announcement for Project AirFi","id":9733,"title":"CKB Eco Fund | Spark program Announcement for Project AirFi","slug":"ckb-eco-fund-spark-program-announcement-for-project-airfi","posts_count":2,"reply_count":0,"highest_post_number":2,"image_url":null,"created_at":"2025-12-12T13:46:59.815Z","last_posted_at":"2025-12-12T14:04:16.125Z","bumped":true,"bumped_at":"2025-12-12T14:04:16.125Z","archetype":"regular","unsee